hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1672","**\nNarrated to us Salamah ibn Junadah: Narrated to us Waki’ (who said): Narrated to us Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah: Narrated to us Humayd ibn Hilal: Narrated to us Abu Burdah: On the authority of al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah (RA) who said:\n\nI ate some garlic, then I came to the Prophet (ﷺ). I found that he had already preceded me by one rak’ah. When he finished the prayer, I stood to make up the missed rak’ah. He perceived the smell of garlic and said:\n\n“Whoever eats this plant, let him not approach our mosque until its smell has gone.”\n\nWhen I finished making up the prayer, I came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I had an excuse.” He extended his hand to me, and I found it to be soft. So I took his hand and inserted it into my sleeve up to my chest, where I found it to be bandaged. He said:\n\n“Indeed, you have an excuse.”\n\n---"
